meta {
  name: POST Ingest Signal (Paper PRICE_UPDATE)
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/webhook/{{paperWebhookToken}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "comment": "paper-secret-1",
    "type": "PRICE_UPDATE",
    "symbol": "SBIN",
    "price": 838
  }
}

tests {
  test("Status 200 (synchronous, not queued)", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("Marks the open position", function() {
    const b = res.getBody();
    expect(b.type).to.equal("PRICE_UPDATE");
    expect(b.marked).to.equal(true);
  });
}

docs {
  Run after **ingest-sell-partial** (position is long 6 @ avg 821.5). Unlike
  ORDER_SIGNAL, PRICE_UPDATE never touches the queue — it's applied
  synchronously and returns 200 (not 202) immediately, with no `paper_orders`
  or `paper_trades` row and no cash movement. It only updates `last_price` and
  recomputes `unrealized_pnl` on the matching open position:
  (838 - 821.5) * 6 = 99.

  `marked` is `false` (not an error) when there's no open position for
  `symbol` — e.g. run this against a flat account and it's a no-op 200.

  Check Paper Trading → positions right after this (before running
  ingest-close, which will overwrite last_price/unrealized_pnl with its own
  fill) to see last_price 838 / unrealized_pnl 99.

  **Deliberate design note:** PRICE_UPDATE is a universal manual override —
  it works exactly the same regardless of which `MARKET_DATA_PROVIDER` is
  configured (`signal` or `fyers`) and never checks that setting. If FYERS is
  connected and has a live quote for this symbol, the mark you just set here
  is transient — the next background sweep (`MARKET_DATA_SNAPSHOT_INTERVAL_SEC`,
  default 45s) will overwrite it with the real FYERS price. If FYERS has no
  quote yet (not connected, market closed), your manual value persists until
  one does. This is intentional (confirmed 2026-07-04) — PRICE_UPDATE stays
  available as a manual override/testing tool even with a real feed
  configured, rather than being blocked or gated by the provider setting.
}
